WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.329
Scenario: A data analyst has permanent administrator access to

2
00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:06.658
payroll, identity management and production infrastructure, although their role

3
00:00:06.658 --> 00:00:09.986
only requires read-only access to one reporting dataset. Safest

4
00:00:09.986 --> 00:00:13.315
response: Option B: Remove unnecessary privileges, grant a named

5
00:00:13.315 --> 00:00:17.014
read-only role for the required dataset and review access periodically.

6
00:00:17.014 --> 00:00:20.342
Access should be limited to the minimum necessary resources

7
00:00:20.342 --> 00:00:23.671
and authorizations for assigned tasks. Option A is unsafe

8
00:00:23.671 --> 00:00:27.000
because Shared privileged accounts reduce accountability and do not

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.329
implement least privilege. Option C is unsafe because Trust

10
00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:33.658
does not replace role-based need, segregation of duties or

11
00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:36.986
periodic authorization review. Option D is unsafe because Unused

12
00:00:36.986 --> 00:00:40.315
privilege remains available for accidental misuse or account compromise.

13
00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:43.644
In practice: Use named accounts and scoped roles, remove

14
00:00:43.644 --> 00:00:46.973
excess privileges, segregate incompatible duties and schedule access recertification.

15
00:00:46.973 --> 00:00:50.301
Key takeaway: Grant each identity only the access needed

16
00:00:50.301 --> 00:00:53.630
for its assigned function, and review it as roles

17
00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:54.000
change.
